# Several turns of a small counted loop are written out one behind the other. They poll once together, and the loop that is left for the last turns polls once a turn
# FORM: AsRead
# OPTIONS: heat=EverythingIsHot disable=pass:InlineCalls
# A loop poll is a load that faults where the target has that, and a comparison with a call on its slow path elsewhere.
# RUN(X64): generate-code
# REQUIRES(X64): x86_64 faulting-loop-polls
# RUN(ARM64): generate-code calls
# REQUIRES(ARM64): arm64
# STATISTIC: LoopsUnrolled >= 1
# X64: f1: size={{*}} polls=3
# ARM64-LABEL: f1: size=
# ARM64: operation operationAOTPollSlow x3
# PROGRAM-OF: rotated-loop.ir
